WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Wednesday,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.440
the eighteenth of November.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.640
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.000
Russia's seaborne crude exports
have climbed to their highest weekly

5
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.920
rate since June, as Ukrainian drone
damage pushes barrels out of its

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.200
refineries and onto tankers.

7
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.880
In the Gulf, American jets
struck an Iranian missile site,

8
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.840
yet Brent kept sliding on fears of a glut.

9
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.120
On the markets. Brent traded at
ninety-one dollars seventy a barrel early

10
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.907
Tuesday, and West Texas
Intermediate at eighty-five dollars,

11
00:00:33.013 --> 00:00:34.880
both below Monday's close.

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.440
Front-month Title Transfer
Facility gas, or TTF,

13
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.960
rose two percent to eighty-six
euros a megawatt hour.

14
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.600
EU gas storage was seventy point
two percent full on the sixteenth of

15
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.400
November. And the American Petroleum
Institute estimates US crude stocks

16
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.320
rose five point three million barrels
in the week to the thirteenth.

17
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.880
Starting with Russia. In the week
to the fifteenth of November,

18
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.800
Russia loaded just over thirty
million barrels of crude for export.

19
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.427
That cargo went out on
thirty-nine tankers,

20
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:05.813
according to Bloomberg.

21
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:09.320
That works out to about four
point three million barrels a day.

22
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.400
It's a rise of nine hundred and fifty
thousand barrels a day on the week

23
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.360
before, and the four-week average
reached three point nine million.

24
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.480
The reason is at home. Ukrainian drone
strikes have knocked out refining

25
00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.000
capacity, so crude that would have
been run domestically is going to

26
00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.560
sea instead. On Tuesday, Ukraine
said it hit two more refineries deep

27
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.480
inside Russia. That's
Ukraine's claim alone,

28
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.560
and no damage has been reported.

29
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.840
At the same time, the EU's
latest shadow-fleet package,

30
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.240
adopted Monday, adds twelve individuals
and one hundred and one entities,

31
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.680
including companies in the
United Arab Emirates and China.

32
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.400
It now reaches oil
buyers, not just owners,

33
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.600
managers and insurers. More barrels
chasing a shrinking pool of willing

34
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.960
ships and buyers could mean wider
discounts on Russia's Urals crude.

35
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.480
For tanker owners still in the
trade, there's more cargo to carry,

36
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.240
and the buyers still taking Russian
oil have more of it on offer.

37
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.440
Over to the Gulf. American warplanes
hit an Iranian missile launch site

38
00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.560
on Qeshm Island on Tuesday.

39
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.000
That comes from a US military
official speaking to Bloomberg.

40
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.813
There's no Iranian account in
the reports we've seen today,

41
00:02:15.867 --> 00:02:17.560
and damage isn't known.

42
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.240
Separately, Iran targeted
US bases in Bahrain.

43
00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.800
Iran's foreign minister also met his
Omani counterpart in Muscat on Tuesday.

44
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.920
Oman says the two discussed keeping
sea corridors secure and reviving

45
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.240
channels for negotiation, but no
concrete arrangement was announced.

46
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.320
Meanwhile, a US Central Command
task force is still working to choke

47
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.360
Iran's land-border and
Caspian supply routes.

48
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.360
Shipping is taking the hits.

49
00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.440
The Panama-flagged liquefied petroleum
gas tanker TARA GAS came under

50
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.480
repeated attack in the
strait, gCaptain reported.

51
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.453
One Indian seafarer is missing
and two crew are in hospital.

52
00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.627
The full crew of twenty-five
was forced off the ship.

53
00:02:57.653 --> 00:03:00.613
There's a supply problem
building behind that too.

54
00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:04.480
According to Tankertrackers dot com,
fewer empty tankers are now sailing

55
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.520
in to load Middle East crude.

56
00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.040
Without that ballast
tonnage, the tracker says,

57
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.040
the recent recovery in
Gulf flows is at risk.

58
00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.040
That matters most to the producers
and buyers who'd been counting on

59
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:15.800
it.

60
00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.480
Turning to gas. TTF's rise on Tuesday
followed a seven percent drop on

61
00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.693
Monday. OilPrice dot com put the
bounce down to the Hormuz attacks,

62
00:03:24.747 --> 00:03:28.640
the strikes on Bahrain, and forecasts
of a cold spell over much of Europe

63
00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.560
from later this week. Storage slipped
by about a quarter of a point on

64
00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:33.480
the day.

65
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.040
With more than two-thirds of Qatari
liquefied natural gas flows still

66
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.600
stifled, Europe is
outbidding Asia for cargoes.

67
00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.320
That lifts prices in both regions,
and it's Asian buyers who are cutting

68
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.880
back. In Germany, coal and lignite
plants now hold twenty-nine of the

69
00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.120
top thirty power-plant
margins, according to Kpler.

70
00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.053
The country's fourth floating import
terminal has also started operating,

71
00:03:56.107 --> 00:03:58.213
which completes its federal programme.

72
00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:01.787
Back to crude, where the weight
of supply is the bigger story.

73
00:04:01.813 --> 00:04:05.360
The American Petroleum Institute's
build follows a nine million barrel

74
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.960
rise the week before, and it also
reports a substantial gasoline build.

75
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.200
The EIA's latest official figures are
for the week to the sixth of November.

76
00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.680
They put commercial crude stocks at
about four hundred and fourteen million

77
00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.160
barrels, and distillates at about
one hundred and three million.

78
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.520
The EIA also expects US crude output
to average nearly fourteen million

79
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.320
barrels a day this quarter.

80
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.200
That weakness in the Atlantic
Basin is now pushing crude east.

81
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.560
Forties differentials in the North
Sea have fallen to levels not seen

82
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.200
since twenty twenty, according to Kpler.

83
00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.360
Suezmax freight is lower too, so
shipping Forties to Ningbo in China

84
00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:45.840
now pays. Vitol has chartered the
Front Classic to carry about a million

85
00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.440
barrels there, good news for North
Sea sellers short of buyers closer

86
00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.200
to home.

87
00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.800
And in the Black Sea, a second
gas carrier has gone down.

88
00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.760
An LPG tanker sank off
Bulgaria's coast on Tuesday,

89
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.120
according to the Bulgarian
defence ministry.

90
00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.560
That was a few dozen miles from
Monday's sinking after a drone attack.

91
00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.280
Separately, all nineteen crew of
StealthGas's Liberia-flagged Gas Husky

92
00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.400
were airlifted off after
a suspected drone attack.

93
00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.840
It was the second serious incident
in the western Black Sea in under

94
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.720
a day, Splash twenty-four seven reported.

95
00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.080
A few more things.

96
00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.320
Chevron is reportedly close to buying
a majority stake in Blackstone-backed

97
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.880
deepwater assets in the Gulf of Mexico,
including Beacon Offshore's Shenandoah

98
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.040
interests. The business is valued
at about five billion dollars,

99
00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.400
though for now this rests
on media reports only.

100
00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.240
Japan has proposed an Asian
crude-stockpiling task force,

101
00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.600
